<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n701" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁγν-εύω</span></b> , pf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥγνευκα</span> D.l. citand., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>consider as part of purity, make it
				a point of religion</i>, c. inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁγνεύουσι ἔμψυχον μηδὲν κτείνειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.140
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i>to bepure</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρνιθος ὄρνις πῶς ἂν ἁγνεύοι φαγών</span>”
				<i>;</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					226
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				6.51
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				837c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				15.6
			</span></i>: c. acc. rei, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χεῖρας ἁ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IT</u>
					1227
				</span></i>
			; <i>keep oneself pure from</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					22.78
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Sto.Herc.</u>
				339.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Am.</u>
				5
			</span></i>; also in 
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυναικός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>GDI</u>
					3636.43
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Cos</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>perform religious ceremonies, officiate</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				1201.6
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B. C.)</span>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				149.8
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii/iii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>purify</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν νοῦν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Sto.Herc.</u>
					339.20
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁγνίζω</span>
			, <i>purify</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antipho
					2.3.11
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				978
			</span></i>(<span class="entity">Cnidus</span>): c.gen., <i>purify
			from</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ παντὸς ἁγνεύων</span>, of
			Epicurus, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Lib.</u>
				p.26O.
			</span></i></div>
